1. Are Java Streams limited to Collections, or can they be used with other data sources?

   1. No, Java Streams are not limited to Collections. They can work with arrays, files, I/O sources, generated values and other data sources.
   2. Collection: list.stream()
   3. Array: Arrays.stream(numbers)
   4. File: Files.lines(Path.of("data.txt")), which returns a Stream<String>.

   Examples:

   // Collection
   List<Integer> list = List.of(10, 20, 30);
   list.stream().forEach(System.out::println);

   // Array
   int[] numbers = {10, 20, 30};
   Arrays.stream(numbers).forEach(System.out::println);

   // Generate stream
   Stream.iterate(1, n -> n + 1)
         .limit(5)
         .forEach(System.out::println);

